--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Relationship to Hermes Agent
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

jev-governor contains no source code from Hermes Agent
(https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent, Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research,
MIT License). It is a standalone package.

The adapter in src/jev_governor/adapters/hermes.py interoperates with Hermes by
calling its public-facing agent object, and docs/install-hermes.md describes a
small patch a user applies to their own Hermes checkout. Neither copies nor
redistributes Hermes source.

This package supersedes an earlier approach that forked Hermes Agent outright.
The fork carried the whole upstream tree in order to add roughly 670 lines, which
meant every upstream release had to be merged rather than simply installed
alongside. A standalone package integrates architecturally instead: a host
protocol with six methods, so the decision layer and the agent framework can be
versioned, tested, and upgraded independently of one another.

